# Open Power Menu @OPM_VERSION@ native bundle

Source commit: `@OPM_SOURCE_COMMIT@`. `bundle.json` seals every payload file and
records the distribution, CPU and build-time dependency versions. Use only the
bundle matching your supported distribution and the accompanying SHA-256 file.
Do not treat an Actions review artifact as an approved stable release.

Run `bash install.sh` from the extracted `native-bundle` directory as your normal
Plasma user. It checks compatibility before changing the installation. The
native runtime, Configure editor, standalone menu, Plasma widget, input plugin,
icons and desktop integration are included; Python/PySide6 is not required.

The installer preserves user menus, shortcuts and panel layout. Keep this
bundle for `bash install.sh --rollback`, `--recover` or `--uninstall`. Remove the
OPM widget through Plasma before uninstalling; retain the original launcher.
Do not delete recovery snapshots or unrelated dependencies as cleanup.

**Power actions can execute immediately.** The KDE setting, OPM Power Actions
preference and explicit custom commands determine behavior. Test with private
mock services; do not use live power actions merely to check installation.

